---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Website Strategy, SEO & Analytics | Brighter Sites"
  description="Understand what helps a professional website perform: custom structure, technical SEO, search visibility, analytics, domains, and ongoing website management."
>
  <section class="page-intro strategy-intro">
    <div class="container strategy-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Website strategy</p>
        <h1>A website can be online without really working for your practice.</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="strategy-lead">
        <p>
          A website builder can give you the tools to publish pages. The harder
          part is deciding what those pages should say, how they should connect,
          how search engines should understand them, what visitors do after they
          arrive, and what should change as the practice grows.
        </p>
        <p>
          This page explains the reasoning behind the technical setup,
          analytics, search work, and ongoing management Brighter Sites offers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container strategy-split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">DIY builder vs. managed website</p>
        <h2>The software is only one part of the job.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="strategy-copy">
        <p>
          Platforms such as Wix can absolutely produce a functional website,
          and they may be a good fit for someone who wants to design, write,
          configure, test, measure, and maintain the site themselves.
        </p>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites is different because you are not only paying for access
          to website-building tools. You are paying for someone to make the web
          decisions with you and carry them through—from page structure and
          mobile behavior to launch setup, search visibility, analytics, and
          ongoing improvements.
        </p>

        <div class="comparison-grid">
          <article>
            <p class="comparison-label">DIY platform</p>
            <h3>You receive the tools.</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>You choose the template or visual direction.</li>
              <li>You decide what pages and content are needed.</li>
              <li>You configure SEO, analytics, domains, and integrations.</li>
              <li>You decide whether the site is performing well.</li>
              <li>You identify and make future improvements.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="comparison-featured">
            <p class="comparison-label">Brighter Sites</p>
            <h3>You receive the site and the web work behind it.</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Custom structure and design around your practice.</li>
              <li>Technical setup and launch handled with you.</li>
              <li>Search and analytics systems configured intentionally.</li>
              <li>A person who can interpret what the site is doing.</li>
              <li>Optional ongoing management to keep improving it.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading strategy-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Search visibility</p>
        <h2>SEO is not one switch we turn on.</h2>
        <p>
          Search performance comes from many small pieces working together. No
          website platform, developer, or SEO company can honestly guarantee a
          particular Google ranking. What we can do is give the site a strong
          technical and content foundation and keep improving it based on real
          information.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="strategy-card-grid">
        <article class="strategy-card">
          <h3>Clear page structure</h3>
          <p>
            Each important service, practitioner, location, or topic needs a clear
            place in the site so visitors and search engines can understand what
            the practice offers.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="strategy-card">
          <h3>Useful page content</h3>
          <p>
            Search engines need enough meaningful information to understand a
            page. We organize content for real people first while making the
            subject and purpose of each page clear.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="strategy-card">
          <h3>Technical SEO</h3>
          <p>
            Page titles, descriptions, headings, canonical URLs, crawlability,
            internal links, sitemaps, and other technical details help search
            engines index the correct pages correctly.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="strategy-card">
          <h3>Mobile and performance</h3>
          <p>
            A site should load quickly and remain easy to use on a phone. That
            matters for prospective clients and supports a healthier technical
            foundation for search.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="strategy-card">
          <h3>Local search signals</h3>
          <p>
            For local practices, the website, Google Business Profile, business
            information, location language, and other local signals should all
            reinforce the same real-world practice identity.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="strategy-card">
          <h3>Measurement after launch</h3>
          <p>
            Search Console and Analytics help show what people search for, how
            they reach the site, which pages they use, and where opportunities
            may exist to improve the site further.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container strategy-split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why analytics matters</p>
        <h2>A dashboard is not the same thing as an answer.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="strategy-copy">
        <p>
          Installing Analytics or Search Console is useful, but the value comes
          from reviewing the information over time and deciding what it means
          for the practice.
        </p>

        <div class="signal-list">
          <div>
            <h3>Are people finding the site?</h3>
            <p>Search impressions, clicks, traffic sources, and location trends can help answer that.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Are they finding the right pages?</h3>
            <p>Page traffic and navigation behavior can show whether important services are being discovered.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Are visitors taking the next step?</h3>
            <p>Appointment requests, contact actions, portal clicks, and other conversion paths help show whether the site supports the practice goal.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>What should we improve next?</h3>
            <p>The useful outcome of analytics is a prioritized decision—not a monthly spreadsheet full of numbers.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="strategy-note">
          This is the reason Managed Growth includes both analysis and website
          work. Finding an opportunity only matters if someone can act on it.
          Managed Growth clients also receive a written website report each
          month so the findings, trends, priorities, and next recommendations
          are clear without having to interpret the raw dashboards themselves.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section domains-section">
    <div class="container domain-panel">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Domains and web addresses</p>
        <h2>Should you buy more than one domain?</h2>
        <p class="domain-lead">
          Sometimes. But extra domains are usually a branding decision, not an
          SEO shortcut.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="domain-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>Good reasons for extra domains</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Protecting the same practice name under common extensions.</li>
            <li>Owning an obvious spelling variation or common typo.</li>
            <li>Preventing confusion with a closely related name.</li>
            <li>Keeping a former domain when rebranding so old visitors still reach you.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>What extra domains do not do</h3>
          <p>
            Buying several versions of the same name does not multiply your
            Google ranking. We normally choose one primary domain for the real
            website and redirect the additional domains to it. That keeps the
            practice identity and search signals centered on one canonical site.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p class="domain-cost-note">
        Domain registration and renewal fees are third-party costs. Some domains
        cost very little; premium names and certain extensions can cost much
        more. We review the available options and costs with you before anything
        is purchased.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="container strategy-split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Ongoing management</p>
        <h2>A good launch is the beginning, not the last time anyone looks at the site.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="strategy-copy">
        <p>
          Practices change. Search behavior changes. Services are added. Staff
          changes. A page that seemed clear at launch may underperform six
          months later. Ongoing management gives the website an owner on the web
          side of the business instead of letting it become a static project.
        </p>

        <div class="management-flow" aria-label="Managed website improvement cycle">
          <span>Measure</span>
          <b>→</b>
          <span>Interpret</span>
          <b>→</b>
          <span>Prioritize</span>
          <b>→</b>
          <span>Improve</span>
        </div>

        <p>
          You remain responsible for the practice decisions. Brighter Sites can
          remain responsible for translating those decisions into website work
          and watching for web-specific issues or opportunities you should know
          about.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container honest-panel">
      <p class="eyebrow">What we will not promise</p>
      <h2>No fake guarantees.</h2>
      <p>
        We will not promise that a website will rank first on Google, guarantee a
        specific number of clients, or imply that custom code automatically
        outranks Wix or another platform. Search results depend on competition,
        geography, content, reputation, time, and many factors outside any web
        developer's control.
      </p>
      <p>
        What we can promise is thoughtful implementation, clear measurement,
        transparent recommendations, and a website that can be improved based on
        what we learn.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Want the web side handled?</p>
        <h2>Build a site you can understand—and a strategy you can keep improving.</h2>
        <p>
          We can start with a new website, improve an existing one, or help you
          decide which setup and ongoing services actually make sense for your
          practice.
        </p>
        <div class="strategy-actions">
          <a class="button" href="/contact/">Start a conversation</a>
          <a class="text-link light-link" href="/services/">View pricing & services →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .strategy-hero-grid,
  .strategy-split {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .strategy-intro h1 {
    max-width: 14ch;
  }

  .strategy-lead,
  .strategy-copy {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .strategy-lead p + p,
  .strategy-copy > p + p,
  .honest-panel p + p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .comparison-grid,
  .strategy-card-grid,
  .domain-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .comparison-grid article,
  .strategy-card,
  .domain-grid article {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: white;
  }

  .comparison-featured {
    border-color: rgba(39,119,111,.35) !important;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(216,235,230,.45), white 55%) !important;
  }

  .comparison-label {
    margin-bottom: .5rem;
    color: var(--teal-dark);
    font-size: .72rem;
    font-weight: 850;
    letter-spacing: .1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .comparison-grid ul,
  .domain-grid ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: .6rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .strategy-heading {
    max-width: 52rem;
  }

  .strategy-card h3,
  .signal-list h3,
  .domain-grid h3 {
    margin-bottom: .45rem;
  }

  .signal-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .signal-list > div {
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .strategy-note {
    padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--teal);
    background: var(--cream);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .domains-section {
    background: var(--ink);
  }

  .domain-panel {
    color: #d6e4e1;
  }

  .domain-panel h2,
  .domain-grid h3 {
    color: white;
  }

  .domain-panel .eyebrow {
    color: #9fd1c8;
  }

  .domain-lead {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
  }

  .domain-grid article {
    border-color: rgba(255,255,255,.12);
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.06);
  }

  .domain-cost-note {
    max-width: 58rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);
    color: #b7cbc7;
    font-size: .92rem;
  }

  .management-flow {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: .65rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    color: var(--teal-dark);
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .management-flow span {
    padding: .45rem .7rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--teal-light);
  }

  .honest-panel {
    max-width: 54rem;
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: white;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
  }

  .honest-panel h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .strategy-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .light-link {
    color: white;
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .strategy-hero-grid,
    .strategy-split {
      grid-template-columns: .85fr 1.15fr;
      align-items: start;
    }

    .comparison-grid,
    .domain-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    .strategy-card-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>